WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:21.541
"Hi! I heard you guys are detectives."

2
00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:25.507
Henry glanced up from pouring a cup of lemonade.

3
00:00:25.508 --> 00:00:29.439
So did his cousin, Maggie, and his best friend, Cole.

4
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:35.703
It was a hot summer day in Belltown, and the kids' lemonade stand was busy.

5
00:00:35.704 --> 00:00:38.372
A girl named Gail was standing there.

6
00:00:38.373 --> 00:00:44.319
Gail was a year ahead of Henry and Cole in school and three years ahead of Maggie.

7
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.589
"Yes, we are detectives!" Maggie told her.

8
00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:54.106
"We solve all mysteries, large and small. See our new sign?"

9
00:00:54.107 --> 00:00:58.333
There were two handmade signs hanging by the lemonade stand.

10
00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:01.032
The first sign was about the lemonade.

11
00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:05.367
The second sign was about the stand's latest business.

12
00:01:05.368 --> 00:01:08.259
It said: The Lemonade Detectives

13
00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.952
All Mysteries Solved, Guaranteed

14
00:01:10.953 --> 00:01:13.954
No Problem Too Large or Too Small

15
00:01:13.955 --> 00:01:17.848
$5 per case plus expenses

16
00:01:17.849 --> 00:01:25.708
Henry thought the new sign looked great, but so far it hadn't brought any customers with mysteries to solve.

17
00:01:25.709 --> 00:01:31.900
The other sign, however, had brought plenty of people looking for a cold glass of lemonade.

18
00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:36.293
"Do you have a mystery for us?" Cole asked Gail eagerly.

19
00:01:36.294 --> 00:01:42.839
"No, my sister just told me that you three are detectives now," Gail said.

20
00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.868
"I'd like to buy some lemonade though."

21
00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:51.626
Maggie looked disappointed. "Are you sure you don't have a case for us?

22
00:01:51.627 --> 00:01:55.445
Hasn't anything mysterious happened to you lately?"

23
00:01:55.446 --> 00:01:58.451
"Nope. Sorry," Gail said.

24
00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:01.502
Henry reached for the lemonade pitcher.

25
00:02:01.503 --> 00:02:05.218
He poured some into a cup and handed the cup to Gail.

26
00:02:05.219 --> 00:02:11.495
"That will be 25 cents, please," he told her. "Enjoy your lemonade."

27
00:02:11.496 --> 00:02:17.890
"Thanks." Gail handed him a quarter. "Good luck with your detective agency."

28
00:02:17.891 --> 00:02:21.134
After she left, Henry sighed.

29
00:02:21.135 --> 00:02:26.556
"I'm starting to think that there are no more mysteries to solve in Belltown."

30
00:02:26.557 --> 00:02:32.513
"We've been sitting here all morning, and haven't gotten a single case!" Cole added.

31
00:02:32.514 --> 00:02:35.476
"We could have been playing soccer instead."

32
00:02:35.477 --> 00:02:40.502
"At least we're making money." Maggie fanned herself with her hand.

33
00:02:40.503 --> 00:02:45.473
"It won't be long before I have enough to start horseback-riding lessons!"

34
00:02:45.474 --> 00:02:50.677
Maggie had started the lemonade stand because she wanted to take riding lessons.

35
00:02:50.678 --> 00:02:54.923
Her parents had told her they would only pay half the cost.

36
00:02:54.924 --> 00:02:58.827
She needed to earn enough money to pay the other half herself.

37
00:02:58.828 --> 00:03:02.902
The lemonade stand was a success right from the start.

38
00:03:02.903 --> 00:03:07.336
Maggie had made plenty of money selling her delicious lemonade.

39
00:03:07.337 --> 00:03:11.851
But then all her money had disappeared right out of her cashbox!

40
00:03:11.852 --> 00:03:15.257
Henry and Cole had helped her track down the thief.

41
00:03:15.258 --> 00:03:19.311
That was when the idea for The Lemonade Detectives was born.

42
00:03:19.312 --> 00:03:24.265
"We'd be making a lot more money if we had a case," Cole grumbled.

43
00:03:24.266 --> 00:03:28.640
"Besides Henry and I never agreed to be lemonade salesmen.

44
00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.548
We want to be detectives!"

45
00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:36.381
"Detectives need to be patient," Maggie shot back.

46
00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.924
"Sooner or later we'll get a case and then—"

47
00:03:39.925 --> 00:03:46.167
"Stop arguing, you two," Henry said. "Here come some more customers."

48
00:03:46.168 --> 00:03:49.116
A group of boys was heading their way.

49
00:03:49.117 --> 00:03:54.566
"Four lemonades, please," one boy said, holding out a dollar bill.

50
00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:58.117
"Here you go." Maggie poured their lemonade.

51
00:03:58.118 --> 00:04:03.256
"Did you know that we offer detective services now as well as lemonade?"

52
00:04:03.257 --> 00:04:06.366
The first boy squinted at the new sign.

53
00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:12.631
"How can you guys be detectives?" he asked. "You're just kids."

54
00:04:12.632 --> 00:04:18.722
A boy named Ryan, who never went anywhere without his skateboard, was standing there too.

55
00:04:18.723 --> 00:04:23.896
"I bet it's because they figured out who stole Maggie's money," he said.

56
00:04:23.897 --> 00:04:26.759
"They thought it was me at first!"

57
00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:33.642
He began telling his friends about how he'd been a suspect as the boys walked away sipping their lemonade.

58
00:04:33.643 --> 00:04:39.883
"At least people are hearing about our detective agency," Maggie said, watching them go.

59
00:04:39.884 --> 00:04:42.653
"That's good," Henry said.

60
00:04:42.654 --> 00:04:47.485
"But I don't think all three of us need to stay here for the whole day."

61
00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:55.025
Cole nodded. "Henry and I could go play soccer, and you could call us if someone shows up with a mystery."

62
00:04:55.026 --> 00:05:01.027
"No way!" Maggie said. "I need you to help me with the lemonade."

63
00:05:01.028 --> 00:05:06.965
"If we aren't here, it means you get to keep all the lemonade money," Henry reminded her.

64
00:05:06.966 --> 00:05:10.375
Maggie hesitated, thinking about that.

65
00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:18.002
"Here comes your next lemonade customer, Maggie," Cole said, pointing down the street. "He's all yours."

66
00:05:18.003 --> 00:05:21.482
Henry glanced at the boy hurrying toward them.

67
00:05:21.483 --> 00:05:24.936
"Hey, it's Nathan," he said.

68
00:05:24.937 --> 00:05:28.409
"Maybe we should see if he wants to play soccer with us."

69
00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:32.819
Nathan was a kid in Henry and Cole's class who lived nearby.

70
00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:37.782
Everyone liked him because he was always friendly, nice, and happy.

71
00:05:37.783 --> 00:05:43.111
When he got closer, though, Henry saw that Nathan didn't look very happy right now.

72
00:05:43.112 --> 00:05:47.334
In fact, he was frowning and looking worried.

73
00:05:47.335 --> 00:05:51.817
"What's up, Nathan?" Cole asked when Nathan reached the lemonade stand.

74
00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:57.385
Nathan pulled a five-dollar bill out of his pocket and slapped it down on the table.

75
00:05:57.386 --> 00:06:06.162
"I've got a mystery for you!" he announced.
